      "notes": "Base status only - new/open/pending/hold pass, solved/closed are blocked. Deliberately enumerates the states we refuse to write to, so a new custom status cannot silently start blocking replies."
    },
    {
      "id": "3ae3ca55-172e-4fc7-9c1d-dbd819d3ba5e",
      "name": "Skip: ticket already solved or closed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        674,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "notes": "Terminal. Reached when a duplicate or replayed webhook targets a ticket the automation has already finished. No Zendesk write on purpose - reopening it would re-queue it for agents and could re-fire the 2nd-message trigger."
    },
    {
      "id": "3fad800e-98b2-4ee7-b13a-b4412a60d8a0",
      "name": "Sticky Status Guard",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        192,
        432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Status guard\n\nBlocks writes when the ticket is already `solved` or `closed`.\n\nWhy: Zendesk can deliver the same `ticket created` webhook a second time hours later (seen 2026-07-23, ~8h37m late). The automation then re-ran on the original first email and contradicted its own earlier reply.\n\nWhy base `status` and not a custom status id: the ticket API always returns `status` as a plain string, so this needs no `cs_project_config` column and behaves identically for every brand. `closed` is covered for free.\n\nA legitimate customer follow-up is safe here - Zendesk auto-reopens a solved ticket on requester reply, so status is `open` by the time the 2nd-message flow runs.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "225539df-c1f1-4503-a447-ef7569ba4bc8",
      "name": "Tag as automation replied",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
